 "notes": [
  "No davwheat seed existed for SK; compiled from scratch, mostly from RÚ's individual-licence decisions.",
  "Jul 2025 multiband auction (ended 9 Jul 2025, €506,073,499.99) covered 800, 900, 1500, 2100, 2600 FDD and 2600 TDD. Terms run 1 Jan 2029–31 Dec 2048, except 1500 MHz (immediate) and 2100 MHz (from 8 Sep 2026). The 2029 layouts are separate future entries.",
  "RÚ's Jan 2025 market assessment (Table 2) gives holdings as sums of both directions: O2 246.4, Orange 300.4, Slovak Telekom 366.8 and SWAN 136 MHz, before the 2025 auction. The current totals here differ because of the 2100 re-award and the 1500 MHz SDL.",
  "900 MHz stays fragmented (100–200 kHz GSM-era pieces) until 2029, and is drawn from RÚ's 2024 renewal decisions.",
  "Current 800 MHz edges come from spectrum-tracker only; they match the 2029 layout RÚ awarded.",
  "Orange provides national roaming to 4ka (2G/3G/4G), which RÚ reports as 5 MHz of 900 and 10 MHz of 2100.",
  "O2 Slovakia's owner is e& PPF Telecom Group (e& controlling stake confirmed by the verifier)."
 ],
